course: dictionary
lesson: 7520
title: Names in history
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Powhatan is a name, so it starts with a capital letter. It can name a person, a people, or a place. Dictionaries mark names like this as proper nouns, and you can often tell one by its capital letter.
explain: Powhatan was a leader of many tribes in what is now Virginia, USA, around 1600. He was the father of Pocahontas, who appears in the story of the English settlement of Jamestown in 1607.
explain: «North America held many Indigenous nations, such as the Haudenosaunee, Cherokee, Lakota and Powhatan, who made treaties, traded and fought with Europeans.» Here Powhatan names one of those nations. Look at the words around it for clues: treaties and trade tell you it was a group of people, not a single person.
fact: A proper noun is the name of a particular person, place or thing, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Powhatan» can mean a person, a people or a place, so the words around it show which one is meant.
fact: Powhatan was the leader of a large group of Algonquian-speaking tribes in what is now Virginia, USA, around 1600.
fact: The Powhatan are the Native American people of that union of tribes, and they have their own language.
fact: «Chief Powhatan», «the Powhatan people» and «the Powhatan Confederacy» show the name used in three different ways.
exercise: Powhatan starts with a capital letter. What kind of word is it? | A describing word | A word for something you can eat | An action word | *A name for a person, people or place
exercise: «Powhatan was the leader of a large group of tribes in what is now Virginia.» Who was Powhatan? | A kind of food | *A leader of a large group of tribes | A small town near the sea | A river in the USA
exercise: Who was the father of Pocahontas? | Her brother | Her teacher | Her neighbour | *Powhatan
test: Is «Powhatan» a common noun or a proper noun? | Adjective | Common noun | *Proper noun | Verb
test: In «the Powhatan people», what does Powhatan name? | *A people | A place only | A colour | An action
exam: Which year is linked with the English settlement of Jamestown in the story of Pocahontas? | *1607 | 1812 | 1066 | 1950
